# Hamilton project configuration. `key=value` per line; `#` starts a comment;
# the value is the literal text after the first `=`.
#
# test_command  the test suite, run from the project root by `hamilton check`.
#               Must exit 0 on success. Use `python -m pytest`, not bare
#               `pytest`, so the project root is importable from the tests.
# paths.<method>  space-separated dirs holding the tests for one verification
#               method defined in `## Verification methods` in
#               spec/requirements.md, e.g. `paths.browser=tests/browser`. A
#               `@covers` tag counts for an AC only under the paths of one of
#               its methods. `manual` needs no paths.
#               Which framework runs and where each method's tests live are
#               build-time calls, so `test_command` and the `paths.*` keys are
#               the keys the agent MAY edit during a `build` session.
# mutation_command  RESERVED. Per-language mutation testing (see concept.md
#               5.3). Not implemented yet -- if you set it, `hamilton check`
#               prints a notice every run and does NOT run it. Leave it unset.

test_command=
# paths.unit=tests/unit
# paths.browser=tests/browser
# mutation_command=
